# My own
#
# Pattern syntax:
# - Plain pattern (e.g., "foo")       -> matches at ANY depth
# - ^/pattern (e.g., "^/foo")         -> matches ONLY at root level
# - Use \. to match literal dots (e.g., "\.txt" not ".txt")
# - Regex wildcards: .+ (one or more), .* (zero or more), ^ (start), $ (end)
#
# Examples:
# - "\.justfile"     ignores .justfile everywhere (nested too)
# - "^/\.justfile"   ignores .justfile only at package root
# - ".*\.log"        ignores all .log files at any depth

